{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"records\":[{\"exampleId\":\"S101-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"609a08e569e0ebdcdf1056a63041f10afd1010380a7a5e272c56a606fcb9cb30\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 claims prior hardship; A3 judges B a beginner; A5 prescribes A's coping method.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 judges B2's immediate reading, but A5 answers B4's difference with a largely repeatable command.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 wants immediate information and B4 asserts an individual way of coping.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 intensifies the condescension after B4 without materially developing the tea prescription.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1's 'failed opening' and reviews suggest a performance but leave the occasion indistinct.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'beginner's relationship' earns its condescension; A5's 'inventing suffering' is less concrete.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":81},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Your first restaurant review? When mine came, I made tea before opening it.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I've opened it. Two stars. I'm ringing the critic.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"That's the stage where I unplugged my phone. Milk?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I've already dialled.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then let it ring while the tea brews. You're rushing a mistake I took all afternoon over.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A converts having endured hardship first into authority to prescribe coping and grade B's reactions.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"S106 competes for greater sympathy through greater pain; S101 claims superior qualifications to guide someone else.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A3 calls B a beginner and A5 recommends A's method, making the claimed advantage instructional rather than a demand for sympathy.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a now uses urgent practical intervention between restaurateurs; alternative b turns a departing colleague's good news into another mentoring opportunity.\",\"reason\":\"The original B4–A5 link repeated the prescription. The revision introduces a restaurant review and an imminent call. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3 maps B's reaction onto A's coping history); logic 5 (B2's call prompts unplugging advice, B4's dialling prompts delay); relationship 4 (B2 and B4 pursue immediate contact); heightening 4 (A5 supervises an underway mistake); specificity 5 (A1 names the review); brevity 4 (A5's afternoon comparison follows the game). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; model review only.\",\"reservation\":\"A5 needs protective sincerity; a sneering delivery would reduce experienced guidance to generic superiority.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S101-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"481f5510878d3ad8c2c494c5c83ec5d8713778f45159992f9c2702653beeae0f\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes earlier redundancy as authority; A3 diagnoses optimism and A5 extends the advice.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 interprets B2's excitement; B4's new job makes A5 switch from leaving to starting over.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 correct A's assumptions without entering a contest over who suffered more.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 expands A's claimed expertise when B4 removes the presumed unemployment crisis.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's redundancy and slow desk tidying establish an immediately playable workplace departure.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'Early stage' efficiently converts B2's happiness into evidence for A's diagnosis.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":90},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I went through redundancy before you. First, tidy your desk slowly.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'm actually excited to leave.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Early stage. I recognise the optimism.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I have another job. They want me there Monday.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Monday? I started too soon after mine. Leave a mug here; you're not ready to make a clean break.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A uses prior hardship to claim continuing authority over how B should understand and handle a transition.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Pain competition would make B's redundancy an occasion to demand sympathy for A's worse experience.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 diagnoses B's optimism and revised A5 prescribes leaving a mug based on A's earlier restart; neither asks B to attend to A's suffering.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b turns a colleague's prompt recovery into grounds for prescribing a slower emotional departure; frozen alternative a intervenes in an urgent call through a coping ritual.\",\"reason\":\"Preserved the original firstPass exactly. The supplied later review identified A5's generic promise of advice; revised B4 adds Monday and A5 now demonstrates that advice through a mug left behind. Workplace setting preserved. Separate internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1 claims seniority, A3 diagnoses optimism, A5 judges readiness from experience); logic 5 (B2's excitement becomes A3's stage, B4's start date prompts A5's slower separation); relationship 4 (B4 supplies concrete evidence against A's diagnosis); heightening 4 (A5 turns successful reemployment into a reason to retain a foothold at the old desk); specificity 4 (A1's desk and A5's mug make the guidance playable); brevity 4 (A5's clean-break advice grows from the departure). Total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; model review only.\",\"reservation\":\"Leaving a mug is impractical advice, so A must sincerely believe that keeping a small connection helps recovery; otherwise the ending can read as merely obstructive.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S102-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"0f975e8b9c898b1a2e6db1a420f8083df355f7f525eb574335ea0e345e76ac55\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 politely suppresses hurt and A5 makes B's attention feel overdue, though A3 becomes conspicuously arch.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 responds to B2's disappointment diagnosis, but A5 treats B4's repair offer as if B had only just noticed.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B4 offers repair, yet A5 supplies no concrete way for that offer to change the relationship.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A5 adds another reproach after B4 without developing the ticket or the proposed repair.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 clearly establishes a forgotten concert and an unused ticket.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'amount of spare ticket' feels verbally manufactured beside A1's natural disappointment.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":65},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You forgot the concert. That's all right. I kept your ticket until the interval.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Let me take you next week.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"That's kind. I'll buy mine, and you can decide nearer the time.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'll buy both. Put it in my calendar now.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Both tickets. How lovely. I'll put my name in the reminder too.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A makes restrained hurt and carefully limited trust motivate B to offer more than A directly requests.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Open guilt-tripping or sarcasm states the grievance aggressively instead of allowing restrained disappointment to exert pressure.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A1's 'quite all right' masks hurt; revised A3 lowers reliance on B, and A5's careful praise carries the remaining doubt.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a makes a forgotten outing produce increasing commitments; alternative b makes a late family call produce a smaller, more dependable promise.\",\"reason\":\"The original repair offer went unused. Internal reread of the revision, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3's reduced trust and A5's qualified praise); logic 5 (B2's invitation prompts separate tickets, B4's calendar prompts a named reminder); relationship 4 (B4 offers practical accountability); heightening 4 (A5 extends doubt into the reminder); specificity 5 (A1's interval anchors the loss); brevity 4 (A5's praise carries the sting). Total 92. Concert setting preserved; five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\"reservation\":\"A5 can sound cutting if heavily emphasized; quiet relief mixed with doubt better preserves the instruction.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S102-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"968a424592711e8ae6a532846a53d005473b1e05930bebe412ac8268933998d4\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 explicitly lowers expectations and A5 offers cautious praise, although A1 announces the technique.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 uses B2's hour and A5 responds to B4's proposed earlier call.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 briefly defends the lateness, then B4 supplies a repair without adding a meaningful constraint.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 repeats lowered expectations after B4 rather than making the new promise consequential.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 identifies a promised call but no relationship or practical consequence; A3's resized hour is abstract.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1's 'lowering my expectations gently' and A3's adjusted hour sound composed rather than conversational.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":70},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Lovely to hear from you, love. I took the phone to bed at nine.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Mum, my shift ran late. I'll call at eight tomorrow.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Eight would be lovely. I won't keep the evening clear.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I can promise ten minutes on my break.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Ten minutes. That's thoughtful. I'll save the important things.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A communicates hurt through modest expectations and careful appreciation that quietly increases the significance of B's promise.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Simply complaining about lateness would make an explicit demand; this card influences through the weight of what A appears willing to accept.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A5 calls an earlier call a 'pleasant surprise'; revised A3 releases the evening while A5 loads ten minutes with important matters.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b gives a working child a real time constraint and a parent restrained longing; alternative a negotiates trust through tickets and a calendar.\",\"reason\":\"Replaced the abstract hour language with a family call constrained by shift work. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3 lowers expectations and A5 carefully praises); logic 5 (B2's eight prompts A3's evening, B4's ten minutes sets A5's limit); relationship 4 (B2 explains work and B4 offers a feasible break); heightening 4 (A5 concentrates important matters into that break); specificity 5 (A1's bedside phone and B2's 'Mum'); brevity 4 (A5 implies the pressure). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\"reservation\":\"The final line may also express healthy prioritization; the earlier disappointment must remain audible without melodrama.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S103-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"82b0f73a0fbfc638b6ed034f34d1c74d57a410cda67b737f0fc9590159b33cef\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 revives their shared bookshop plan; A3 and A5 repeatedly return to its two chairs under present constraints.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"B2's rent concern shrinks A3's proposal to chairs; B4's tiny flat makes A5 defer the sea.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 voice credible shared financial and spatial limits that shape A's hopeful compromise.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 turns A1's remembered aspiration into a present commitment to sit together despite B4's cramped flat.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1's napkin plan, A3's drawn chairs and B4's tiny flat give actors a clear shared world.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'Sea later. Chairs together now' compresses the practical and emotional compromise.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":92},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"This napkin still says we'll open a bookshop by the sea.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"We drew that before rent became real.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"We also drew two chairs. We could start there.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Only if we get rid of your desk.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Sell it. Put 'funding our seaside bookshop' in the listing. We're making room for the first two customers.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A repeatedly uses a specific hope once shared with B to find emotional footing inside present limitations.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"S110 revives A's own earlier hopeful self; this card depends on a remembered aspiration belonging to both people.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A1's 'we'll open' and A3's 'We also drew' establish joint history; revised A5 uses that same shared bookshop to understand losing the desk.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a sacrifices personal furniture to make a domestic fragment of the shared shop real; revised alternative b accepts an affordable substitute for their anniversary destination while preserving the promised swim.\",\"reason\":\"Preserved the original firstPass exactly. The supplied later review found A5 mostly repeated A3's chairs. Revised B4 makes the chairs cost A a desk, and A5 accepts that cost while returning to the shared shop in the sale listing and imagined customers. The shared-home setting remains; the desk sale is new illustrative pressure. Separate internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1, A3 and A5 repeatedly return to their joint plan); logic 5 (B2's rent prompts a smaller start, B4's desk condition prompts selling it); relationship 4 (B4 makes A bear a concrete cost); heightening 4 (A5 commits property and publicly labels its purpose); specificity 4 (A1's napkin and B4's desk anchor the exchange); brevity 4 (A5 makes the couple their own first customers). Total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; model review only.\",\"reservation\":\"The first customers are metaphorical because the immediate project is two chairs at home. A needs to find comfort in that shared imagining rather than imply a functioning shop already exists.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S103-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"fb7f94205256889ecdf268762cc3fb9d74f345ebcf5b184f51e1468ac003b8c3\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 recalls the jar's shared summer-trip purpose; A3 and A5 preserve that hope after B2 reports the money gone.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 distinguishes the idea from B2's spent money; A5 answers B4's request for a present contribution.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 supplies a financial setback and B4 shifts into constructive participation.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 moves from A3's symbolic preservation to restarting the shared saving with one coin.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's jar of spare buttons makes the abandoned trip visible and playable.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'jar kept the idea' and A5's 'old job' sustain one economical image.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":86},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Remember when this jar was for our anniversary at the seaside?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"We spent the money on the boiler.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"We promised we'd swim together. The boiler didn't cancel that.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"That's in three weeks. We can afford the bus to the reservoir.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then put the bus fare in the jar. I'll pack the towels; we're still coming home with wet hair.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A treats the remains of a shared earlier plan as a place to return emotionally when present resources disappoint.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Generic optimism can propose any better future; this behavior specifically restores a hope A and B already held together.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Revised A1 recalls their anniversary jar, A3 returns to their promised swim after the boiler expense, and A5 preserves that shared outcome through B's cheaper destination.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b lets B help preserve the shared swim through a practical substitute destination; revised alternative a accepts a personal sacrifice and keeps the larger bookshop dream present in a furniture sale.\",\"reason\":\"Preserved the original firstPass exactly. The supplied later review found the final coin slight and the jar personification repetitive. Kept the trip jar but added an anniversary, boiler expense and affordable reservoir outing. Separate internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1 recalls their plan, A3 and A5 recover its shared promise); logic 5 (B2's expense prompts preserving the swim, B4's bus option determines A5's fare and packing); relationship 4 (B4 contributes a feasible alternative within their resources); heightening 4 (A5 commits to the actual outing instead of only preserving an idea); specificity 5 (A1's anniversary, B2's boiler and B4's reservoir define the compromise); brevity 4 (A5's wet hair makes the surviving hope tangible). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; model review only.\",\"reservation\":\"The development is affectionate and practical, with gentle wit. The anniversary and swimming promise are new illustrative details rather than facts inherited from the original seed.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S104-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"6e2613aa328c36093f8be0759e3c177f8a00516ef0d14e2f744c6d37c21664ac\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 invokes B's past scarf loan to earn honesty, and A3 values B's staying over fixing things.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 directly uses B2's inability to fix everything; A5 answers B4 but repeats A1's unspecified honest answer.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 limits the rescuer role and B4 asks what support A actually needs.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A5 restates the demand for unprotected honesty without identifying a new consequence after B4.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A1 specifies a scarf and a bad night but never establishes what present question B must answer.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's weather comparison economically distinguishes presence from repair, though A5 stays abstract.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":76},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You lent me this scarf when my marriage ended. Tell me honestly: should I answer his message?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I can't decide that for you.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You didn't decide anything that night. You stayed. Tell me what worries you.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"That you'll spend tonight waiting for another message.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then stay while I leave it unanswered. I'll make us tea this time.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A treats comfort previously received from B as an enduring bond that can now support honesty, patience and returned care.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"S107 depends on B's reassuring reactions to feel safe; S104 invokes a history of care as grounds for a continuing reciprocal bond.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A1 names the scarf loan and A3 recalls B staying; revised A5 adds returned hospitality after receiving B's honest concern.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a seeks candid advice about contact with an ex and then shared company; alternative b turns a former shopkeeper's request into support for B's own uncertainty.\",\"reason\":\"Added a concrete present dilemma about an ex's message. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1 invokes comfort, A5 reciprocates); logic 5 (B2's boundary prompts concerns instead, B4's waiting concern prompts leaving the message unanswered); relationship 5 (B2 limits responsibility and B4 offers specific honesty); heightening 4 (A5 asks for sustained company); specificity 5 (A1 names the decision); brevity 4 (A5's tea carries reciprocity). Total 95. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\"reservation\":\"The newly specified separation gives the scene emotional weight; it is a clear playable example with only gentle wit.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S104-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"276b19a66c8453a38a39083ed16b3a9f6a3506f2679fd7c567588f5552549e9a\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 invokes B's support through the shop closing; A3 uses their shared silence to permit honest uncertainty.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 accepts B2's not knowing; A5 accepts B4's request to sit, although the original 'maybe' remains unexplained.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 cannot supply an answer and B4 offers presence, which A5 recognizes as valuable.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 validates the sitting offered in B4 but adds little beyond A3's permission for silence.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A1's shop closure establishes history but not the present request receiving a 'polite maybe'.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'whole hours of it' makes silence concrete without a separate explanation.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":79},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You sat with me when my shop closed. Will you help at the new stall? An honest answer.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I don't know. My own shop's struggling.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then forget the stall. You let me talk for hours when mine went.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Could we sit without talking first?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Of course. You gave me three silent evenings. I've kept this one free.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A uses the memory of B's past comfort to establish a bond that now warrants candid answers and reciprocal patience.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Calling in a favor treats past care as a debt payable to A; this card also allows that history to generate care flowing back to B.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A3 permits B's uncertainty because they endured silence together; revised A3 releases the stall request and A5 returns that patient presence.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b reverses who currently needs support after B's disclosure; alternative a keeps A as the person in difficulty while adding a smaller reciprocal gesture.\",\"reason\":\"Specified the unanswered request and gave B a present problem. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 turn past comfort into returned support); logic 5 (B2's struggling shop redirects A3, B4's silence sets A5's offer); relationship 5 (B2 reveals competing need and B4 chooses the support); heightening 4 (A5 commits an evening); specificity 5 (A1's new stall); brevity 4 (A5's counted evenings embody patience). Total 95. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\"reservation\":\"A5's availability is newly revealed and should sound like willing generosity rather than a suspiciously convenient prepared speech.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S105-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"90c0f0b46bc0f9e02365c1b8dc350c1cb00958373e48e7a804c176b11475569d\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 serves everyone and volunteers for calls; A3 minimizes shaking; A5 resists B's offered care.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 converts B2's shaking concern into a reason calls remain possible; A5 responds to B4's invitation to sit.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 notices A's physical strain and B4 offers to take over the actual task.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"After B4 removes the calling burden, A5 claims a further duty to appear in control.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's tea and difficult calls, followed by B2's shaking hands, establish an active domestic crisis.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's distinction between calls and trays makes the denial follow A's practical logic.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":86},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I've made everyone tea. I'll call Dad's friends about the funeral.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Your hands are shaking.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then it's good the calls don't require trays.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Sit down. I'll call. Just give me their numbers.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I'll dial for you. Peter will cry; I'll stay on the other phone in case you need rescuing.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A protects the role of steady caretaker by minimizing visible strain and finding another responsibility whenever B offers relief.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Ordinary helpfulness accepts useful assistance; this card specifically resists becoming a recipient of care.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 dismisses B2's evidence of shaking, and revised A5 converts B4's takeover into a reason to dial and monitor the call for B's sake.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a retains responsibility by supervising a practical task B offers to take over; frozen alternative b declines physical comfort by reserving B's shoulder for a child.\",\"reason\":\"Preserved the original firstPass exactly. The supplied later review found the crisis generic and A5's remaining duty indistinct. Added funeral notifications and a named friend; B4 now requests numbers, giving A5 a concrete route back into the calls. Separate internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1 serves others, A3 minimizes distress, A5 resists relief); logic 5 (B2's hands prompt the tray distinction, B4's request for numbers prompts dialling and supervision); relationship 4 (B4 offers actual replacement while needing contact details); heightening 4 (A5 makes the proposed carer another person requiring rescue); specificity 5 (A1's funeral and A5's Peter define the task); brevity 4 (A5's rescue offer follows A's protective logic). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; model review only.\",\"reservation\":\"The other phone implies a household extension. Both alternatives now involve bereavement, so their distinction rests on task control versus refusal of intimate comfort, not a different occasion.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S105-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"3708a8b87a129b7b34a4c854521ef9fe7df8eaf84fd87930a635f7fc08e03573\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 gives away the last tissue, A3 minimizes tears, and A5 redirects B4's care toward everyone else.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2's observed crying; A5 inverts B4's offer but uses no specific form of proposed care.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 express concern but offer little personal need or concrete intervention for A to handle.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 restates the caretaker priority at a broader scale without a new practical consequence.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 supplies a tissue and sleeve, but neither A1 nor B2 locates the shared tears in a situation.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'Efficiently' gives A's self-denial a compact resource-management logic.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":78},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Take the last tissue. Mum's funeral was hard on you. I've got my sleeve.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"You're crying into both sleeves.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"They're washable. How's your daughter holding up?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"She's asleep. Come here. You can cry on my shoulder.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You'll need that shoulder when she wakes. I'll get you a dry cardigan.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A maintains strength for other people by discounting personal distress and converting offers of comfort into further caretaking.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Stoicism can simply conceal emotion; this card actively steadies others and resists their attempts to provide care.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A1 gives B the tissue and A5 redirects B's care; revised A5 preserves B's shoulder for the child and supplies clothing.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b uses physical intimacy and family responsibilities; alternative a uses practical delegation and the appearance of collective control.\",\"reason\":\"Added a funeral and a sleeping child to make care concrete. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3 minimizes tears and A5 rejects comfort through service); logic 5 (B2's sleeves prompt washability, B4's shoulder prompts preserving it); relationship 4 (B4 offers physical comfort and resolves the child's current need); heightening 4 (A5 invents future caretaking grounds); specificity 5 (A1's funeral); brevity 4 (A5's cardigan follows the wet-sleeve problem). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\"reservation\":\"The funeral setting makes the humor delicate; A's concern for B must remain real for the redirection to land.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S106-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"848b1058f68aeab7c8d59b3c32c894874d5d592b131d294029918c28e70f0ca9\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 weighs B's single rejection against fourteen, A3 establishes a scale, and A5 claims time for A's pain.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2's request for personal attention; A5 turns B4's rejection of competition into a claim on listening time.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 wants to discuss this rejection and B4 challenges the comparative framework.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 converts A1's numerical comparison into an obligation to hear all fourteen stories.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's retained rejection letters give the emotional comparison a tangible count.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'establish the scale' exposes A's sincere measurement logic in a short reply.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":86},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"One publisher turned you down? I've kept fourteen rejection letters.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Can you put them away? I came here for a hug.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Of course. Though fourteen rejections ought to qualify me for more than one.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Come here. We can both have the same hug.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Hold on after I let go, then. I've got thirteen more to get through.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A measures B's disappointment against accumulated personal suffering to claim a larger share of emotional attention.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"S101 uses hardship as authority to guide coping; S106 uses it to establish whose feelings should occupy more space.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Revised A1 compares fourteen rejections with one, A3 claims extra comfort, and A5 makes B's reciprocal hug continue for A's remaining disappointments.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a converts an offered mutual hug into unequal physical reassurance; frozen alternative b bargains over scarce conversation time using unemployment duration and an interview.\",\"reason\":\"Preserved the original firstPass exactly. The supplied later review found a loose inference from B4's noncompetition objection to A5's listening claim. Specified publishing rejections and replaced that objection with a shared hug, which A5 can directly redistribute. Separate internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1 counts disappointments, A3 and A5 claim proportionate comfort); logic 5 (B2's requested hug determines A3's entitlement, B4's equal hug prompts A5's unequal release); relationship 4 (B2 seeks comfort and B4 offers mutual care); heightening 4 (A5 turns equality into continued service for thirteen more hurts); specificity 4 (A1's publisher and B2's hug make the encounter playable); brevity 4 (A5's thirteen follows the established fourteen rather than adding another comparison). Total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; model review only.\",\"reservation\":\"A's hug arithmetic is deliberately self-serving. The unequal release must express a sincere need for extra comfort, not merely a clever way to defeat B's offer.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S106-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"13519411893504ca29f4a9e75daa05f9a49a561c4e6ef08ba0f66f97fdc67dbc\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 compares a week with a year; A3 preserves the twelve-month advantage; A5 minimizes B's suffering again.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2's wish to finish, but A5's quieter-Tuesday comparison could follow many replies besides B4's request to listen.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 both ask to be heard, giving A little new pressure on the second exchange.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 sharpens the insult but repeats A1's duration comparison rather than changing its consequences.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A1's rough week and rough year never identify an actual disappointment or concrete situation.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's quieter Tuesday is compact and card-related, though more detachable than A3's response.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":72},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You've been unemployed a week. I've been out a year. This coffee should really be for me.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I bought it so you'd listen to what happened.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I'll listen. Mine will take longer; there's twelve months to cover.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Ten minutes each. I've got an interview.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"An interview already? Then give me fifteen. You've started recovering.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A turns comparative suffering into an asserted entitlement to greater time and sympathy.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Experienced mentoring would use A's year without work to help B; this behavior uses the year to claim the coffee and more listening time.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A5 makes B's week smaller than A's Tuesday; revised A5 treats B's interview as grounds for reallocating sympathy to A.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b bargains over a fixed conversation window and B's improving prospects; alternative a demands cumulative attention for a stack of past rejections.\",\"reason\":\"Introduced unemployment, a purchased coffee and an interview deadline. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1 and A5 allocate care by comparative hardship); logic 5 (B2's listening purpose prompts duration, B4's interview changes A5's allocation); relationship 5 (B4 sets a limit for a credible appointment); heightening 4 (A5 claims fifteen of the available twenty minutes); specificity 5 (A1's coffee and unemployment); brevity 4 (A5's recovery diagnosis earns the bargain). Total 95. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\"reservation\":\"A's numerical fairness is intentionally distorted; the actor should pursue recognition sincerely rather than enjoy humiliating B.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S107-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"a7f40f6eea3f5f145167a86d0cf974cb8be9167e87cac84cd6ea4d23378491dc\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 relies on B's reassuring face, A3 claims independence while preserving it, and A5 reacts to B's uncertainty.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2's independence challenge with a conditional demonstration; A5 uses B4's uncertainty to protect the reassuring expression.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 encourages independence and B4 honestly limits what B can know about the letter.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 wants B's face insulated from B4's admitted ignorance, increasing A's control over the reassurance.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a seated companion and an unopened letter with an immediately playable dependency.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's face 'hearing' B4's admission gives a compact physical expression to A's safety measure.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":90},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Stay seated while I open this letter. Your face looks reassuring.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"You can open it without me.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Certainly. Keep looking like that while I prove it.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I don't know what's inside.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You weren't supposed to let your face hear that.\"}],\"decision\":\"retained\",\"mechanism\":\"A gauges safety through one particular person's expression while insisting that dependence is smaller than it plainly is.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Generic reassurance-seeking only asks for comfort; this card makes B's reactions the safety instrument and includes A's downplaying.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 claims to prove independence while requiring B's expression, and A5 treats a change in that expression as the problem.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a tries to preserve B's reassuring face despite uncertainty; revised alternative b becomes ready to act after B smiles and credits the furniture.\",\"reason\":\"Retained unchanged after internal reread. Both B replies alter how A maintains the facial reassurance, and A3 supplies the necessary denial of dependence. Original coach-1.0 ratings stand.\",\"reservation\":\"The letter's contents remain unspecified, and A5's personification needs a light touch to avoid sounding like a prepared joke.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S107-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"9b2f250a9bbff02676852cde66bc8ddde7401f8bc675084167f2195c0d0a6043\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 and A3 deny needing B nearby, but neither establishes B's reactions as A's measure of safety.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 denies B2's nervousness diagnosis and A5 responds with relief to B4's promise to stay.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 identifies the dependency and B4 accommodates it without a distinct reaction for A to interpret.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 repeats the viewing-angle excuse after B4, with little new commitment beyond satisfaction.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 names 'the result' and seating but leaves the event and source of uncertainty undefined.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'emotionally practical' describes the evasion too explicitly, and A5 repeats its angle metaphor.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":64},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Sit beside me while I open the audition result. You've stopped smiling.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'm squinting at the screen. You haven't opened it.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Right. So nothing's wrong. Move closer; the text is small.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'm smiling now. Whatever it says, we'll get lunch.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"There. I can click it now. This chair was the problem.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A interprets B's visible reactions as evidence of safety, then attributes the resulting confidence to an ordinary practical adjustment.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Wanting companionship during a result is broader than this card; the distinguishing behavior is using B's reaction as a gauge and minimizing its effect.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A5 shows relief from presence only; revised A1 notices a lost smile, A3 infers safety from its explanation, and A5 credits the chair.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b lets B's supportive smile produce forward action; alternative a resists B's honest uncertainty to preserve a reassuring expression.\",\"reason\":\"Specified an audition result and made facial reactions causal. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3 reads safety and A5 disowns the smile's effect); logic 5 (B2 explains the expression, B4's smile enables clicking); relationship 4 (B2 corrects the inference and B4 offers lunch); heightening 4 (A5 becomes willing to open the result); specificity 5 (A1's audition screen); brevity 4 (A5's chair excuse completes the denial). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\"reservation\":\"B4 explicitly reports smiling because the example permits spoken turns only; performance may make that line feel slightly demonstrative.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S108-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"e1cf8b5ba7ac903666d532ebe8ae7c1cd606a2c176a2fd737f3046ad60740386\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 avoids harmless blue cups, A3 implies an unwelcome memory, and A5 excessively controls the remaining sightline.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 refuses B2's historical inquiry; B4's offer to put the cup away creates A5's more exact hiding requirement.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 tries to understand and B4 offers accommodation, which A then makes more demanding.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A5 makes even the visible handle unacceptable after B4 agrees to remove the cup.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1's breakfast cups and A5's plates and handle make the avoidance physically precise.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'Nothing breakfast needs to revisit' withholds history economically; A5's handle carries the resulting excess.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":89},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Could we use any cups except the blue ones today?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"What happened with a blue cup?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Nothing breakfast needs to revisit.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'll put it away.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Behind the plates, please. The handle's still looking this way.\"}],\"decision\":\"retained\",\"mechanism\":\"A responds to a harmless reminder of old hurt by controlling increasingly small details of its presence.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"An arbitrary dislike or superstition could also avoid a blue cup, but this card roots the control in something painful returning.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"B2 asks what happened and A3 refuses to 'revisit' it, connecting A5's excessive concealment to implied history.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a contains a reminder through visual concealment; revised alternative b protects a celebration through increasingly exact envelope handling.\",\"reason\":\"Retained unchanged after internal reread. B4's helpful removal directly generates A5's stricter requirement, making accommodation develop the game. Original coach-1.0 ratings stand.\",\"reservation\":\"The old hurt is implied rather than identified, so a purely whimsical delivery could obscure the card's emotional basis.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S108-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"5adeb2b1608f30649fba08cc22938e996c424492885093bef0d808dc081e4162\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A1 avoids a yellow envelope, but B2 identifies a bill and no turn establishes an old hurt rather than present financial stress.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 uses B2's bill to relocate it; A5 explains B4's wiping observation without changing the avoidance.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 corrects A and B4 notices repeated wiping, but neither offers a consequential alternative.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A5 repeats the envelope's exclusion already requested in A1 and A3.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's yellow envelope beside a cake and B4's table wiping establish clear physical business.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'everything except the envelope' is compact but mainly restates A3's relocation.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":53},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Could you move that yellow envelope away from my birthday cake?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"It's a voucher from your sister.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Lovely. My eviction notice came in yellow. I'll find her a nicer envelope.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'll take the voucher out and bin this one.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Thank you. Under the coffee grounds, please. I'll hold the lid.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A overmanages an innocuous present object because one of its details recalls an earlier hurt.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Avoiding a current bill can be ordinary financial anxiety; this card requires the harmless reminder itself to activate old pain.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original B2 makes the envelope a live bill; revised B2 makes it a gift and A3 explicitly ties its yellow color to a past eviction notice.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b combines protective helpfulness with ceremonial disposal; alternative a relies on guarded silence and hiding a cup's remaining handle.\",\"reason\":\"Kept the cake and yellow envelope, changed its contents to a harmless gift, and supplied the old association. Internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3's remembered notice causes replacement); logic 5 (B2's gift prompts a nicer envelope, B4's disposal prompts burial); relationship 4 (B4 preserves the gift while helping); heightening 4 (A5 supervises disposal); specificity 5 (A1's birthday cake); brevity 4 (A5's coffee grounds embody excess). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns under 75 words.\",\"reservation\":\"The eviction reference is direct exposition, though brief; the scene needs care to keep the humor in control of the envelope rather than the past loss.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S109-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"f072d219cf591f67925212eb8201c77d488a341206d090e0152656ec66b962b8\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 resentfully admires B's immediate opening; A3 preserves the image of courage; A5 wants to match B's speed.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 interprets B2's admitted fear as well concealed; A5 rejects B4's offered time in favor of B's example.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 reveals vulnerability and B4 offers patience, both credible attempts to reduce A's self-comparison.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B4's permission to wait prompts A5 to impose B's exact speed as a personal standard.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 places both people with rejection letters and different willingness to open them.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'hid it very efficiently' turns B2's reassuring admission into another enviable achievement.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":86},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You opened your rejection letter straight away. Must be nice, being brave on demand.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I was scared too.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You hid it very efficiently.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Take your time with yours. I'll leave you alone to open it.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"No, stay. I'm opening it now. You shouldn't get to be brave and considerate while I'm still finding the flap.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A experiences B's emotional courage as a model to emulate and an unfair exposure of A's own hesitation.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Simple envy wants B's advantage; this card specifically combines admiration for emotional bravery with resentment of the comparison it creates.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A1 names bravery resentfully, A3 treats hidden fear as an achievement, and revised A5 starts opening the letter while protesting B's further display of consideration.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a turns B's offer of privacy into pressure for A to act immediately with B present; frozen alternative b accepts preparation together while resenting how easily B might perform it.\",\"reason\":\"Preserved the original firstPass exactly. The supplied later review found A5 an envious preference without action. B4 now offers to leave, and A5 keeps B present while beginning the opening and resenting the extra virtue in that offer. Letter setting preserved. Separate internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1 admires bravery resentfully and A5 follows its example while feeling exposed); logic 5 (B2's fear becomes A3's admired concealment, B4's privacy offer prompts A5's stay and consideration complaint); relationship 4 (B4 offers relief rather than a challenge); heightening 4 (A5 commits to opening instead of only wishing to match B); specificity 4 (A1's letter and A5's flap make the action immediate); brevity 4 (A5's fumbling keeps the comparison grounded). Total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; model review only.\",\"reservation\":\"The recipient or purpose of A's letter remains unspecified. A5's complaint about B being considerate must retain its basis in admired courage, rather than become general resentment of every good quality.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S109-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"79ff4c28dabca70eda1ddabe22a620dc6b13746a76015c4c53a7643424933b28\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 explicitly admires and resents B's disclosure; A3 makes even stumbling courageous; A5 accepts help with continued resentment.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 directly revalues B2's stumbling, and A5 specifically responds to B4's practice offer.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 corrects the idealized account and B4 offers a collaborative route into A's own disclosure.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 moves from judging B's past bravery to accepting practice while extending the comparison into it.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes an unrehearsed emotional disclosure and B4 gives the pair a playable activity.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's demand not to make practice look easy follows directly from A3's admiration of imperfect courage.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":90},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You told them how you felt without rehearsing. I resent how impressive that was.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I stumbled over half of it.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Even your stumbling looked courageous.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Want to practise with me?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Yes. Don't make practising look easy too.\"}],\"decision\":\"retained\",\"mechanism\":\"A draws inspiration from B's emotional bravery while resenting how that bravery makes A's own difficulty visible.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Hostile rivalry would refuse or sabotage B's help; this card can accept help while retaining the uncomfortable admiration.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 admires B's stumbling rather than dismissing it, and A5 says yes to B4's practice offer while guarding against another painful comparison.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b turns admiration into cooperative preparation; alternative a converts B's patience into pressure to match B's speed.\",\"reason\":\"Retained unchanged after 